WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.390
"Moon Knight" might not be the most well-known
Marvel character, but he's got a rich history

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.150
in the comics all the same.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:11.490
With a new MCU series about to drop, what
do you need to know about the character and

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.740
the show before you watch?

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:18.330
The official trailer for "Moon Knight" premiered
during the Rams-Cardinals wild card game in

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:24.490
January 2022, and in addition to providing
fans with a sneak peek of what the highly-anticipated

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:28.150
series might entail, it also revealed the
show's release date.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:34.130
"Moon Knight" is scheduled to premiere on
Wednesday, March 30, 2022, and, like the rest

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:39.379
of Marvel's Phase 4 TV series, will stream
exclusively on Disney+.

00:00:39.379 --> 00:00:44.089
As of right now, it's unclear what time the
series will become available for streaming,

00:00:44.089 --> 00:00:48.449
but we can speculate that it will be similar
to the release times of prior Marvel series

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:53.699
like "Hawkeye," "Loki," and "WandaVision,"
which all premiered their episodes at 3:00am

00:00:53.699 --> 00:00:55.429
ET each week

00:00:55.429 --> 00:01:00.499
We also know that "Moon Knight" will consist
of six episodes, according to Kevin Feige.The

00:01:00.499 --> 00:01:06.610
Marvel Studios boss also says that these episodes
will run between 40-50 minutes, which is in

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.970
line with other Marvel Disney+ series.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:14.350
Leading the cast of "Moon Knight" is none
other than Oscar Isaac, who is set to play

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:19.170
the titular hero as well as his multitude
of overlapping personalities.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:24.950
Moon Knight's true identity is that of Marc
Spector, a mercenary who suffers from dissociative

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:30.479
identity disorder, and constantly swaps between
several distinctive identities as the series

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:31.600
goes on.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:36.340
The interesting thing is that these identities
essentially function as totally different

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:41.150
characters, and it'll be interesting to see
how Isaac brings them each to life on screen.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:46.400
Ethan Hawke is also set to appear in the series
as a cult leader named Arthur Harrow, who

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.840
appears in the trailer and encourages Marc
to…

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.390
"Embrace the chaos."

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:58.359
The series also features French actor Gaspard
Ulliel, who appears posthumously as Anton

00:01:58.359 --> 00:02:02.460
Mogart, the alter ego of the character known
as Midnight Man.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:07.791
Ulliel tragically passed away in a ski accident
after filming, and "Moon Knight" was one of

00:02:07.791 --> 00:02:10.280
the last projects he ever worked on.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:15.220
Others confirmed to be in the series include
F. Murray Abraham, who voices the Egyptian

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:21.390
god Khonshu, Lucy Thackerey, who plays a coworker
who is close to one of Marc's many personalities,

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.840
and May Calamawy in an undisclosed role.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:29.180
The official trailer for "Moon Knight" revealed
quite a lot about the story and characters

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.810
that we'll be seeing throughout the series.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:35.570
At the start of the trailer, Marc believes
himself to be a man named Steven who works

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:40.230
at a museum, and admits that he "can't tell
the difference between life and dreams."

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:45.510
He is tormented by strange visions and nightmares
and doesn't even recognize the name "Marc"

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.950
when somebody calls him on the phone.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:49.970
"What's wrong with you Marc?"

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:52.390
"Why did you call me Marc?"

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:57.320
Marc's story is as much about fighting literal
bad guys as it is about fighting his inner

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:01.840
thoughts — and from what we see in this
trailer, it seems like the latter is a losing

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:02.840
battle.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:07.520
After a brief montage of Marc's disturbing
visions, we finally get to see him don Moon

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.520
Knight's iconic white costume.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.690
The suit literally materializes from thin
air around Marc as he looks up at the moon,

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:19.031
indicating that similar to the comics, he
receives his powers from the Egyptian God

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:20.740
of the Moon, Khonshu.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:26.010
Finally, the trailer ends with Marc brutally
beating some monstrous-looking creature before

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.660
turning to the camera.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:32.430
It's an incredible trailer from start to finish,
giving fans just enough to be excited about

00:03:35.376 --> 00:03:40.316
For now, it looks like "Moon Knight" is going
to have two villains: Dr. Arthur Harrow and

00:03:40.316 --> 00:03:41.496
Midnight Man.

00:03:41.496 --> 00:03:46.006
It seems as if the latter will be more of
a secondary baddie, as Ethan Hawke's Harrow

00:03:46.006 --> 00:03:48.456
looks to be the main villain of the series.

00:03:48.456 --> 00:03:53.006
However, it's suspected that there's more
than meets the eye here, given that Dr. Harrow

00:03:53.006 --> 00:03:56.036
has only appeared in one comic book issue.

00:03:56.036 --> 00:03:59.846
There's not that much story in the comic for
the show to pull from, either.

00:03:59.846 --> 00:04:05.096
Many fans believe the persona of Dr. Harrow
is a red herring, and Hawke is actually playing

00:04:05.096 --> 00:04:06.886
the Moon Knight villain Sun King.

00:04:06.886 --> 00:04:13.386
A former Ravencroft Institute patient, Sun
King has a base of loyal followers, much like

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.846
we see Hawke's Farrow have in the trailer.

00:04:15.846 --> 00:04:21.426
Both Sun King and Moon Knight have connections
to Egyptian gods, with the former obsessed

00:04:21.426 --> 00:04:25.796
with Amon Ra and the latter who is blessed
with powers by Khonshu.

00:04:25.796 --> 00:04:31.106
It's also very possible that Hawke's character
is an amalgamation of Dr. Harrow, Sun King,

00:04:31.106 --> 00:04:34.096
and other famous Moon Knight villains.

00:04:34.096 --> 00:04:35.386
Only time will tell.

00:04:35.386 --> 00:04:39.196
What we do know for certain is the inspiration
for Hawke's character.

00:04:39.196 --> 00:04:44.016
In an interview with Seth Meyers, Hawke pointed
to one famous cult leader as the inspiration

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:46.576
for his portrayal of Dr. Harrow.

00:04:46.576 --> 00:04:48.906
"I've based my character on David Koresh."

00:04:48.906 --> 00:04:50.266
"Have you really?"

00:04:50.266 --> 00:04:51.266
"Yes."

00:04:51.266 --> 00:04:55.217
"Moon Knight" will feature three directors
— one of whom directed four episodes, while

00:04:55.217 --> 00:04:58.146
the remaining pair directed the other two.

00:04:58.146 --> 00:05:03.046
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Mohamed
Diab is helming four episodes solo, marking

00:05:03.046 --> 00:05:06.136
the first time he's directed an English-language
project.

00:05:06.136 --> 00:05:12.196
Diab is known in his home country of Egypt
for projects like "Cairo 678" and "Clash,"

00:05:12.196 --> 00:05:15.046
but "Moon Knight" marks his first Hollywood
project.

00:05:15.046 --> 00:05:20.386
Per Variety, the famous directing duo of Justin
Benson and Aaron Moorehead tackled the other

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.646
two episodes.

00:05:21.646 --> 00:05:25.146
The indie-horror visionaries don't have the
longest resumes in the business, but their

00:05:25.146 --> 00:05:26.746
work speaks for itself.

00:05:26.746 --> 00:05:32.096
They directed 2019's "Synchronic" with Anthony
Mackie, an episode of Jordan Peele's "The

00:05:32.096 --> 00:05:37.216
Twilight Zone" reboot, and 2017's "The Endless,"
in which they also starred.

00:05:37.216 --> 00:05:41.116
The higher-ups at Marvel Studios clearly have
been impressed with the work they've seen

00:05:41.116 --> 00:05:45.566
from Benson and Moorehead, as the pair have
also been brought on to direct "a majority"

00:05:45.566 --> 00:05:49.896
of the episodes from the upcoming "Loki" Season
2, according to Deadline.

00:05:49.896 --> 00:05:55.706
So far, every MCU series on Disney+ has been
scripted by a different writer.

00:05:55.706 --> 00:06:00.706
"Moon Knight" will introduce head writer Jeremy
Slater to the Marvel Cinematic Universe, but

00:06:00.706 --> 00:06:04.276
this is far from Slater's first dip in the
superhero pool.

00:06:04.276 --> 00:06:08.776
He penned the script to the 2015 "Fantastic
Four" movie, he's also one of the creators

00:06:08.776 --> 00:06:10.916
of Netflix's "The Umbrella Academy."

00:06:10.916 --> 00:06:15.416
If "Moon Knight" turns out to be anything
like Slater's initial pitch, we're in for

00:06:15.416 --> 00:06:16.416
a treat.

00:06:16.416 --> 00:06:17.416
He told Empire,

00:06:17.416 --> 00:06:21.805
"'Raiders of the Lost Ark' was actually a
big reference when I first pitched.

00:06:21.805 --> 00:06:27.816
How can we tell this dark, complex story but
also inject some big, fun, supernatural, Amblin-style

00:06:27.816 --> 00:06:29.426
magic at the same time?"

00:06:29.426 --> 00:06:34.216
A lot of trust has been put into Slater recently,
which gives us a lot of hope for "Moon Knight."

00:06:34.216 --> 00:06:37.926
He's also penning the script for "Mortal Kombat
2."

00:06:37.926 --> 00:06:42.046
Leading into the premiere, there's no clear
answer on where "Moon Knight" fits in the

00:06:42.046 --> 00:06:45.266
official timeline of the Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:06:45.266 --> 00:06:51.006
As of now, "Hawkeye" is the latest show on
the timeline, taking place in December 2024.

00:06:51.006 --> 00:06:56.516
It's entirely possible that "Moon Knight"
is the first MCU project to occur in 2025

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:58.456
if it takes place right after "Hawkeye."

00:06:58.456 --> 00:07:04.726
It's also possible "Moon Knight" happens sometime
during 2023, as do two other Disney+ live-action

00:07:04.726 --> 00:07:05.726
series.

00:07:05.726 --> 00:07:10.096
"WandaVision" begins three weeks after the
conclusion of "Avengers: Endgame," while "The

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:12.706
Falcon and the Winter Soldier" is about six
months out.

00:07:12.706 --> 00:07:18.176
"Loki" kicks off in 2012, but about 99 percent
of the series occurs in a space outside of

00:07:18.176 --> 00:07:22.386
time, so it really doesn't have a solid place
on the timeline.

00:07:22.386 --> 00:07:26.846
"Eternals," "Shang-Chi and the Legend of the
Ten Rings," and "Spider-Man: No Way Home"

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:32.026
all take place before "Hawkeye," with "No
Way Home" definitely landing in 2023.

00:07:32.026 --> 00:07:35.786
Long story short, "Moon Knight" can fit anywhere.

00:07:35.786 --> 00:07:41.656
Every MCU-Disney+ series has its own identity,
but "Moon Knight" is going to really shake

00:07:41.656 --> 00:07:43.156
things up in a big way.

00:07:43.156 --> 00:07:48.506
Kevin Feige admitted to Empire that things
are taking a major left turn with "Moon Knight,"

00:07:48.506 --> 00:07:51.926
suggesting it's the darkest series in the
MCU to date.

00:07:51.926 --> 00:07:52.926
He told the outlet,

00:07:52.926 --> 00:07:57.186
"It's been fun to work with Disney+ and see
the boundaries shifting on what we're able

00:07:57.186 --> 00:07:58.186
to do.

00:07:58.186 --> 00:08:02.696
There are moments when Moon Knight is wailing
on another character, and it is loud and brutal,

00:08:02.696 --> 00:08:06.186
and the knee-jerk reaction is, 'We're gonna
pull back on this, right?'

00:08:06.186 --> 00:08:07.546
We're not pulling back.

00:08:07.546 --> 00:08:08.895
There's a tonal shift.

00:08:08.895 --> 00:08:10.606
This is a different thing."

00:08:10.606 --> 00:08:16.526
So far, every MCU series has held a TV-14
rating, including the animated project "What

00:08:16.526 --> 00:08:17.526
If...?"

00:08:17.526 --> 00:08:20.916
The way Feige describes "Moon Knight" and
its brutality sounds like the series might

00:08:20.916 --> 00:08:26.466
have earned a more adult rating than its predecessors,
but Disney+ has it labeled with a TV-14 rating

00:08:26.466 --> 00:08:27.846
on its website.

00:08:27.846 --> 00:08:32.955
One thing is clear: "Moon Knight" is certainly
going to push the barriers of how far a TV-14

00:08:32.955 --> 00:08:34.596
show can go.

00:08:34.596 --> 00:08:39.016
For now, it looks like there won't be a second
season of "Moon Knight," but that's based

00:08:39.016 --> 00:08:41.646
on a small comment made by Oscar Isaac.

00:08:41.646 --> 00:08:46.565
When speaking with Jared Leto for Variety's
Actors on Actors series, Isaac mentioned that

00:08:46.565 --> 00:08:48.906
"Moon Knight" was a "limited series."

00:08:48.906 --> 00:08:53.466
Limited means just that, so for now, fans
likely shouldn't get their hopes up for a

00:08:53.466 --> 00:08:54.466
second season.

00:08:54.466 --> 00:08:58.646
"WandaVision" was also confirmed to be just
a limited series, but that's not the case

00:08:58.646 --> 00:09:01.296
for all MCU live-action shows.

00:09:01.296 --> 00:09:06.266
So far, "Loki" is the only Disney+ series
from Marvel to have a confirmed Season 2.

00:09:06.266 --> 00:09:10.646
This announcement came in the credits of the
first season's finale episode, so if we are

00:09:10.646 --> 00:09:14.636
getting a follow-up for "Moon Knight," its
finale could be the episode that holds all

00:09:14.636 --> 00:09:15.636
the answers.

00:09:15.636 --> 00:09:20.086
However, just because there might not be a
Season 2 of the series, that doesn't mean

00:09:20.086 --> 00:09:24.045
we won't be seeing Moon Knight again in the
MCU.

00:09:24.045 --> 00:09:28.886
Up to this point, the title characters of
every MCU series had already appeared in multiple

00:09:28.886 --> 00:09:33.266
movies, so there was always the assumption
we'd see them again on the big screen.

00:09:33.266 --> 00:09:37.886
Moon Knight is the first title character to
get their origin story in a Disney+ series,

00:09:37.886 --> 00:09:40.886
and his future afterward is slightly unknown.

00:09:40.886 --> 00:09:45.636
Since we know we probably won't be getting
a Season 2, we'd have to hope Oscar Isaac's

00:09:45.636 --> 00:09:50.416
Marc Spector would show up in future MCU flicks
— and it looks like those hopes are due

00:09:50.416 --> 00:09:51.706
to be fulfilled.

00:09:51.706 --> 00:09:56.796
Kevin Feige confirmed to The Hollywood Reporter
that Moon Knight would appear in an MCU film

00:09:56.796 --> 00:09:58.185
after the series.

00:09:58.185 --> 00:10:02.826
This is also the case for Jennifer Walters
from "She-Hulk" and Kamala Khan from "Ms.

00:10:02.826 --> 00:10:03.826
Marvel."

00:10:03.826 --> 00:10:08.076
For now, your guess is as good as ours as
far as where Moon Knight might appear next,

00:10:08.076 --> 00:10:12.065
but hopefully, we'll get some clues during
the show's six-episode run.

00:10:12.065 --> 00:10:15.966
He isn't one of the characters rumored to
appear in "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse

00:10:15.966 --> 00:10:20.406
of Madness," and there have been no rumblings
of him showing up in "Thor: Love and Thunder"

00:10:20.406 --> 00:10:22.865
or "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever."

00:10:22.865 --> 00:10:27.386
There's no shortage of upcoming MCU movies,
though, so here's hoping we'll get more Moon

00:10:27.386 --> 00:10:29.615
Knight sooner than later.

00:10:29.615 --> 00:10:35.315
Cameos in the MCU are common these days, and
the Disney+ Marvel series are no exception.

00:10:35.315 --> 00:10:40.406
James Rhodes popped in an Emmy-nominated scene
in "The Falcon and the Winter Soldier"; Wilson

00:10:40.406 --> 00:10:45.845
Fisk made his MCU debut in "Hawkeye"; the
X-Men's version of Pietro Maximoff sort-of

00:10:45.845 --> 00:10:50.626
cameoed in "WandaVision"; and Chris Hemsworth
had a very sneaky voice cameo in "Loki" as

00:10:50.626 --> 00:10:56.785
a trapped Frog Thor.

00:10:56.785 --> 00:11:01.035
Needless to say, we're expecting someone we
know to show up in "Moon Knight."

00:11:01.035 --> 00:11:06.356
Rumors abound that Jon Bernthal could be reprising
his role as Frank Castle, aka the Punisher,

00:11:06.356 --> 00:11:07.406
in "Moon Knight."

00:11:07.406 --> 00:11:11.745
Redditors have been hoping for this cameo
for a while now, especially given that Frank

00:11:11.745 --> 00:11:14.476
Castle and Moon Knight have a history in the
comics.

00:11:14.476 --> 00:11:20.365
With Vincent D'Onofrio showing up on Disney+
in an old Netflix role, it's certainly possible.

00:11:20.365 --> 00:11:24.776
There's also speculation Mark Ruffalo might
be appearing as Bruce Banner in "Moon Knight"

00:11:24.776 --> 00:11:29.336
after he was spotted in Budapest, Hungary
during the same time the series was filming

00:11:29.336 --> 00:11:30.336
there.

00:11:30.336 --> 00:11:34.805
If that's true, it seems like there'd be no
better MCU hero to teach Moon Knight how to

00:11:34.805 --> 00:11:37.055
control his emotional issues.

00:11:37.055 --> 00:11:42.476
"That's my secret, Cap, I'm always angry."

00:11:42.476 --> 00:11:45.225
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:45.225 --> 00:11:49.655
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
MCU series are coming soon.

00:11:49.655 --> 00:11:52.685
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

